{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1546042-wraith-chronicles-conversion-guide","id":1546042,"title":"Wraith Chronicles Conversion Guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-17T13:28:04-08:00","id":1546042,"title":"Wraith Chronicles Conversion Guide","content":"Hello everyone. I have made a fan conversion guide to run Wraith: the Oblivion using the Chronicles of Darkness rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1wwn1nu9xeqaiXqX_1QncSiT4_kvYHNMv?usp=drive_link\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1wwn1nu9xeqaiXqX_1QncSiT4_kvYHNMv?usp=drive_link\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1wwn1nu9xeqaiXqX_1QncSiT4_kvYHNMv?usp=drive_link\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1wwn1nu9xeqaiXqX_1QncSiT4_kvYHNMv?usp=drive_link </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is a beta right now, I'm sure I've left in some mistakes. I've also spoken with Mr. Gone, who will eventually be making a character sheet for the conversion, but he's got stuff on his plate currently. I'll include it along with the guide in future when it's complete.<br /> <br /> I love Wraith, it is my all-time favourite RPG, but over time I realized I really wanted to run it in the Chronicles system. Originally, this guide was just meant for my playgroup, but I figured other people might find a use for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Things you may notice:<br /> - This document does not contain setting info, it assumes you're familiar with Wraith's setting. If you're using this guide, you're sort of ignoring the regular rules for ghosts in Chronicles.<br /> - I'm Canadian, so I use british spelling throughout the document. I also went a bit overboard with capitalization. This will be reduced in the final draft.<br /> - This book converts the Arcanoi from Wraith20, Alloyed/Tempered Arcanoi, and some extras, but does not include all the extra Guild Arcanoi from the various Guildbooks.<br /> - There's not a lot in the Book of Oblivion that I was interested in adding to my games, so I did leave some stuff out from it. Mostly I just incorporated some the book's Thorns, the Osseum Arcanos, and some extra pieces here and there.<br /> - I added the Haint Spectre Caste from Doomslayers into the guide, because I like them visually. But I was also wondering whether I should include them at all? I feel like depicting the victims of atrocities as ravening monsters is... tricky. Wraith is a very grim game, and I'm fine with that, but I figured I'd ask what other people thought?<br /> - This thing took Waaaay longer to finish than I thought it would, and I was flagging by the time I got to the Orpheus chapter. It is pretty sparse. Orpheus Shades are not currently a part of this guide, I might add some dedicated rules for them in the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, hope you enjoy it!<br /> <br /> <br /> Jesse Charles Cowell<br /> Occasional writer and artists for None More Dark Publishing<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/browse?keyword=none%20more%20dark\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/brow...%20more%20dark</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3096-lhangdon_rhyme","name":"Lhangdon_Rhyme","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-28T23:43:09-08:00","id":1548017,"title":"","content":"Oh I saw the MrGone post about this! It's really cool what you've done and probably the most progress I've seen for the likes of it! It's inspired me to try and fit Wraith onto/utop the underworld Cosmology seen in CofD. We'll see how far I get though.<br /> The biggest thing I have a question for, if you don't mind, is why does the ranking equivalent limitation on spending the fuel stat only apply to healing? (Unless I just misread... In which case oops!)<br /> Thanks for the work at NMD and on this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T21:49:57-08:00","id":1548319,"title":"","content":"Hi Rexitonic! Thank you so much! I appreciate that a lot.<br /> <br /> The reason I made Pathos per turn only apply to healing is that Wraithly Arcanoi cost wildly varying amounts of pathos to activate, and Arcanoi operate on a lower power scale than many other supernatural powers. So I didn't want it to take 4 turns to activate a pretty middling power.<br /> <br /> Additionally, Pathos is one of the easiest energy stats to fill up. So, I kind of like that some Arcanoi arts eat up a lot of that power. And Wraiths don't really have any equivalent of a vampire's physical intensity, spending a lot per turn doesn't benefit them as much as some other splats.<br /> <br /> I could have gone through and altered the Pathos cost of every Arcanoi, but for the moment that is beyond the scope of the conversion. Maybe in the future I'd make full new versions of each Arcanoi, but that's a LOT to update.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3096-lhangdon_rhyme","name":"Lhangdon_Rhyme","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}